### ML Platform API Testing
### Using VS Code REST Client
### Base URL - Modify as needed
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api/v1
@contentType = application/json

#################################################################
# Health Check
#################################################################

### Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

#################################################################
# GPU Provider API
#################################################################

### List Available GPU Providers
GET {{baseUrl}}/gpu/providers

#################################################################
# GPU Instance Search (Browse Available GPUs)
#################################################################

### Search All Available GPU Instances
GET {{baseUrl}}/gpu/instances

### Search by Provider (ppio)
GET {{baseUrl}}/gpu/instances?provider=ppio

### Search by Provider (vastai)
GET {{baseUrl}}/gpu/instances?provider=vastai

### Search by Provider (local)
GET {{baseUrl}}/gpu/instances?provider=local

### Search by GPU Type
GET {{baseUrl}}/gpu/instances?gpu_type=RTX%204096

### Search with Multiple Filters
GET {{baseUrl}}/gpu/instances?provider=ppio&gpu_type=RTX%204096&max_price=5.0&min_gpus=1

#################################################################
# User Instance Management (Offers API)
# Key endpoints for viewing and managing purchased instances
#################################################################

### 1. List User's Purchased Instances
### Returns all instances rented by the user, with status synced from provider
GET {{baseUrl}}/offers?user_id=default

### 2. Get Single Instance Detail (with live provider status sync)
### Replace {{instance_id}} with actual instance ID from the list above
GET {{baseUrl}}/offers/352b6428-0663-40b8-af4a-e0b584e5e93b

### 3. Create a New Instance Rental (PPIO)
### Step 1: Pick offer_id and provider from /gpu/instances response
POST {{baseUrl}}/offers
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "provider": "ppio",
  "offer_id": "YOUR_PPIO_PRODUCT_ID",
  "user_id": "default",
  "name": "ppio-training-1",
  "image": "pytorch/pytorch:2.1.0-cuda11.8-cudnn8-runtime",
  "disk_size": 100,
  "duration_hours": 24,
  "price_per_hour": 1.5,
  "gpu_name": "RTX 4096",
  "num_gpus": 1,
  "location": "cn-north-1"
}

### 4. Create a New Instance Rental (Vast.ai)
POST {{baseUrl}}/offers
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "provider": "vastai",
  "offer_id": "12345678",
  "user_id": "default",
  "name": "vastai-training-1",
  "image": "pytorch/pytorch:2.1.0-cuda11.8-cudnn8-runtime",
  "disk_size": 50,
  "duration_hours": 12,
  "price_per_hour": 2.0,
  "gpu_name": "RTX 4090",
  "num_gpus": 1,
  "location": "US"
}

### 5. Create a New Instance Rental (Local)
POST {{baseUrl}}/offers
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "provider": "local",
  "offer_id": "local-docker",
  "user_id": "default",
  "name": "local-test-1",
  "image": "ubuntu:22.04",
  "disk_size": 20,
  "duration_hours": 0,
  "price_per_hour": 0,
  "gpu_name": "CPU/Docker",
  "num_gpus": 0,
  "location": "本地"
}

### 6. Stop a Running Instance
### Replace {{instance_id}} with actual ID
POST {{baseUrl}}/offers/{{instance_id}}/stop

### 7. Start a Stopped Instance
### Replace {{instance_id}} with actual ID
POST {{baseUrl}}/offers/{{instance_id}}/start

### 8. Destroy an Instance (permanent)
### Replace {{instance_id}} with actual ID
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/offers/{{instance_id}}

#################################################################
# Task API - Training Task Management
#################################################################

### Create a Training Task
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "mnist-training",
  "description": "MNIST digit classification training",
  "image": "pytorch/pytorch:2.1.0-cuda11.8-cudnn8-runtime",
  "command": "python train.py --epochs 10 --batch-size 64",
  "data_path": "/app/data/mnist/",
  "output_path": "/app/output/mnist/",
  "env_vars": [
    "PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=max_split_size_mb:512",
    "CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0"
  ]
}

### List All Tasks
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks

### Get Task Details
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{task_id}}

### Cancel a Running Task
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{task_id}}

### Get Task Logs (SSE Stream)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{task_id}}/logs?client_id=test-client-1

#################################################################
# Storage API - Object Storage Management (COS)
#################################################################

### List All Files
GET {{baseUrl}}/storage/files

### List Files with Prefix
GET {{baseUrl}}/storage/files?prefix=data/

### Get Presigned Download URL
GET {{baseUrl}}/storage/download-url?key=outputs%2Fmodel.pt

#################################################################
# Example Workflows
#################################################################

### === Workflow: Rent a PPIO GPU Instance ===
# Step 1: Browse available GPU offers
# GET {{baseUrl}}/gpu/instances?provider=ppio
#
# Step 2: Pick an offer and create rental
# POST {{baseUrl}}/offers
# {
#   "provider": "ppio",
#   "offer_id": "<product_id_from_step_1>",
#   "user_id": "default",
#   "name": "my-gpu",
#   "image": "pytorch/pytorch:2.1.0-cuda11.8-cudnn8-runtime",
#   "disk_size": 100,
#   "gpu_name": "RTX 4096",
#   "num_gpus": 1
# }
# (Save the returned instance.id)
#
# Step 3: List user's instances to check status
# GET {{baseUrl}}/offers?user_id=default
# Status flow: creating -> running
#
# Step 4: Query specific instance detail (syncs provider status)
# GET {{baseUrl}}/offers/<instance_id>
# Response includes: status, ssh_host, ssh_port, ssh_user
#
# Step 5: Stop instance when idle
# POST {{baseUrl}}/offers/<instance_id>/stop
#
# Step 6: Restart later
# POST {{baseUrl}}/offers/<instance_id>/start
#
# Step 7: Destroy when no longer needed
# DELETE {{baseUrl}}/offers/<instance_id>

### === Workflow: Check Instance Status After Creation ===
# 1. Create instance
#    POST {{baseUrl}}/offers
#    -> Response: { "id": "inst-xxx", "status": "creating", ... }
#
# 2. Poll instance list (status synced from provider)
#    GET {{baseUrl}}/offers?user_id=default
#    -> Check status field: creating | running | stopped | destroying | destroyed
#
# 3. Query single instance for detailed status
#    GET {{baseUrl}}/offers/inst-xxx
#    -> Returns full instance info with provider-synced status and SSH details
#
# 4. When status is "running", SSH is ready:
#    ssh -p <ssh_port> <ssh_user>@<ssh_host>

